					<div class="col-md-6">
						<h2>Project Background</h2>
						<p>Project Hub was developed in Java using the JavaFX framework for a modern, responsive desktop UI. All user interfaces were designed with Scene Builder, enabling a structured and visual layout approach. The application features consistent and custom styling through CSS, enhancing the look and feel of the JavaFX components.</p>
						<p>The build process is managed with Maven, allowing for organized dependency management and streamlined project configuration. For testing, the project uses JUnit, ensuring reliability and correctness through unit testing of core functionalities.</p>
						<p>This software emphasizes both functionality and presentation, offering a clean interface for users to upload, manage, and explore software projects thus, making it ideal for use as a personal project portfolio platform.</p>
					  
						<h2>About the UI</h2>
						<p><strong>Home Page:</strong> This is the landing screen where users are first greeted. It features a clean welcome message, a login button for returning users, and showcases a few randomly selected public projects to explore. This helps users quickly get a sense of what the platform offers.</p>
						<p><strong>Project Detail Page:</strong> Also known as the “About Your Project” view, this page displays all the information about a specific project. It includes metadata like the project name, summary, author, and date created. It also provides access to browse the uploaded project directory files, making it easy for others to review a project’s contents.</p>
						<p><strong>Account Page:</strong> This is where users manage their profile and projects. From here, users can edit their account information, update profile details, and create new project entries to share on the platform. It serves as a control center for each user's portfolio management.</p>

